# Cloud Security Analyst – Role Guide

## Role Focus
Securing cloud identities, monitoring cloud activity, and identifying misconfigurations.

## Certifications Supporting This Role
- CompTIA Security+
- AZ-900 (cloud fundamentals)
- CCNA (network and cloud connectivity awareness)

## Labs to Review (Recommended Order)
1. 01-beginner-labs/04-cloud-identity/entra-id/01-users-groups-roles
2. 01-beginner-labs/04-cloud-identity/azure/02-logging-sign-in-audit
3. 01-beginner-labs/04-cloud-identity/aws/03-cloudtrail-basics
4. 01-beginner-labs/04-cloud-identity/azure/03-misconfiguration-check
5. 01-beginner-labs/03-salesforce-security/04-login-security-mfa
6. 02-enterprise-context-labs/04-cloud-at-scale/centralized-cloud-logging

## What This Demonstrates
I can monitor and secure cloud and SaaS environments using identity controls, logging, and investigation techniques.

## Where This Role Fits in My Path
Cloud Security Analyst → Cloud Security Engineer

